Why dual-licensed?
──────────────────
Brave Browser itself is licensed under MPL-2.0. Offering MPL-2.0 here means
the licensing of this packaging code is consistent with the software it
packages — anyone working with both can do so under a single license.

GPL-3.0 is included because it is the standard copyleft license for free
software. If you are building something GPL-licensed, you can use this flake
without any license mismatch.

In short: pick whichever license works for your project.

  GPL-3.0  →  see LICENSE
  MPL-2.0  →  see LICENSE-MPL

